                <pb facs="1171" n="1047" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg1047"/>

                <head>No. 642.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fairchild to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-12-29"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 29, 1880</date>.
                        (Rec’d January 15.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 97.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: At an interview had this day with his
                    excellency Señor Elduayen, he desired me to convey to you his best thanks for
                    the kindly consideration which led you to so promptly and emphatically assure
                    the Spanish minister at Washington of the falseness of the construction which
                    had been, by parties in the United States and in Spain interested in fomenting
                    trouble between the two governments, placed upon the words of the President of
                    the United States, in his last message, regarding the late firing upon American
                    vessels by Spanish gunboats in Cuban waters.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>LUCIUS FAIRCHILD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
